{"id":258,"date":"2016-05-16T12:57:44","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:57:44","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/li-ning-china-masters-2011-men-doubles-final-cai-yunfu-hai-feng-vs-jung-jae-sunglee-yong-dae\/"},"modified":"2016-08-31T16:35:52","modified_gmt":"2016-08-31T16:35:52","slug":"li-ning-china-masters-2011-mens-doubles-finals-caiyun-fuhaifeng-jungjaesung-leeyongdae-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/li-ning-china-masters-2011-mens-doubles-finals-caiyun-fuhaifeng-jungjaesung-leeyongdae.html","title":{"rendered":"Li Ning China Masters 2011 men doubles Final: Cai Yun\/Fu Hai Feng vs Jung Jae Sung\/Lee Yong Dae"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float: left;\"><\/div>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"80%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Tournament<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Li Ning China Masters 2011 Final (Super Series)<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Location<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Changzhou, China<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Date<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>18 September 2011<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Category<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Men Doubles<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p>This match between Cai\/Fu and Jung\/Lee has shocked most badminton fans around the world!<\/p>\n<p>China has gained dominance in badminton and since the Li Ning China Masters 2011 was held in China, the Chinese were expected to take all the titles from every category.<\/p>\n<p>However, the Koreans rocked the stadium by winning the first 3 rally points before the Chinese pair got their first point.<\/p>\n<p>Lee Yong Dae and Jung Jae Sung were on perfect form. The Chinese&#8217;s attacks were not very effective against the Koreans in this match.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Jung Jae Sung and Lee Yong Dae<\/strong> have the best defence in men&#8217;s doubles whereas <strong>Cai Yun and Fu Hai Feng<\/strong> has the best and strongest attacks in men&#8217;s doubles.<\/p>\n<p>It was interesting to watch how the best defenders go against the best attackers in the world.<\/p>\n<p>The Chinese pair struggled to find their best form.<\/p>\n<p>Fu Hai Feng made a couple of unforced errors, giving away unnecessary points to the Koreans.<\/p>\n<p>On the other hand, Jung and Lee were very determined to prevent the Chinese from having a clean sweep of titles in their home country, China.<\/p>\n<p>There were a couple of long and exciting rallies where both teams worked so hard to get the point.<\/p>\n<h3>Fully Recovered?<\/h3>\n<p>There was also one thing that I realized in this tournament.<\/p>\n<p>Lee Yong Dae, the young Olympic champion had an ongoing injury. His racket arm was bandaged whenever he attended a tournament.<\/p>\n<p>In this China Masters 2011, there were no bandages or signs of injury.<\/p>\n<p>Has he recovered fully?<\/p>\n<p>One thing was for sure, he could smash harder than before in this finals!<\/p>\n<p>Sit back and enjoy this thrilling final between Cai Yun\/Fu Hai Feng and Jung Jae Sung\/Lee Yong Dae. Watch how the Koreans defeat the Chinese in China.<\/p>\n<p><a href=\"http:\/\/youtu.be\/WY1nlSec03c\" target=\"_blank\">Click here to Watch the Video<\/a><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"osim-bwf-world-superseries-event-2011-season-review.html\">Read the Season Wrap Up of the <strong>OSIM BWF World Superseries Event<\/strong> here<\/a>!<\/p>\n<div class=\"retnvbx1\"><\/div>\n<div class=\"fb-comments-intro-ns\">\n<div class=\"retnvbx\"><\/div>\n<h3><span class=\"teelmeww\">Tell me what you think!<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>What do you think about what you just read? Leave me a comment below.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<div id=\"COMMENTING\" class=\"fb-comment\">\n<div class=\"fb-comments\" data-href=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/li-ning-china-masters-2011-mens-doubles-finals-caiyun-fuhaifeng-jungjaesung-leeyongdae.html\" data-num-posts=\"15\" data-width=\"100%\"><\/div>\n<h3 class=\"fblikeste\">Like Masterbadminton.com?<\/h3>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<div id=\"fb-root